\f0\i0\fs36 \cf9 TL;DR\cf11 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf0 F1 customer is rebootstrapping their Google Distributed Cloud air-gapped (GDCag) deployment to 1.16.2. There has been some deliberation on whether F1\'92s Operations Suite Infrastructure Core version 1 (OICv1) Operations Suite Infrastructure Rack (OIR) will be upgraded vs rebootstrapped. OICv1 represents five GDCag operable components (OCs); EDR, PNET, SIEM, VULN and OIC core. \uc0\u8232 \u8232 Consensus is that F1 will proceed with a rebootstrap vs an upgrade of OICv1. However, to ensure alignment, this document will highlight the reasoning behind this decision, and compares both options with one another.
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sb360\sa80\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf11 Background\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf0 F1\'92s OICv1 OIR was deployed at 1.13.x, then upgraded to 1.14.6. After the upgrade, F1 did not interact with OIC again until 09/2026. As expected, OIC was found to be in an unusable state, and will need to be brought back up 1.16.2 specifications.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs28 \cf11 Requirements for 1.16.2+\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f5\b\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	
\f1 Hyper-V 4TB H: drive 
\f2\b0 - At 1.14.2+, all H: drives must have a capacity of 4TB\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f5\b {\listtext	2.	}2.	
\f1 File server 100GB F: drive 
\f2\b0 - The OIC file server\'92s F: must be at 100GB and be homed it Hyper-V server\'92s H: drive\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f5\b {\listtext	3.	}3.	
\f1 Microsoft Endpoint Configuration Management at current version 
\f2\b0 - MECM must be at the currently available version 2509 or later\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sb360\sa80\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\fs36 \cf0 {\listtext	4.	}Preferred Option: Rebootstrap
\i \cf7 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\i0\fs22 \cf7 {\listtext	5.	}This option represents the shortest path for the customer, and ensures that all product and bugs fixes are properly applied. A reboostrap guarantees product alignment with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "%5Cl%20%22h.ja295f4elq8z%22"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 1.16.2 Requirements}}\cf0  and does not demand additional toil from the F1 team.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\fs28 \cf11 {\listtext	6.	}Advantages\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9679 	
\f6\i\b PNET bootstrap not required\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\i0\b0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9679 	Faster path to success for the customer\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9679 	All product updates and bugs fixes are applied\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9679 	No risk of disruptions due to underlying issues related to staleness\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9679 	Fresh install avoids costly, time consuming, manual intervention to cover {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "%5Cl%20%22h.ja295f4elq8z%22"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 1.16.2 Requirements}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\fs28 \cf11 {\listtext	\'95	}Disadvantages\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9679 	\cf6 Permanent 
\f6\i\b deletion
\f2\i0\b0 \cf0  of all existing OICv1 data\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9679 	Workstations will be re-PXE\'92d, which for F1 is a higher lift than normal due to OIF to OIR bandwidth and latency constraints\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9679 	\cf6 OIC services will be down until the bootstrap is complete\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\fs28 \cf11 {\listtext	\'95	}Procedure\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}The procedure to rebootstrap will be simply to follow our already defined deployment process, but exclude PNET steps with some data collection of the current configuration.\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs24 \cf11 {\listtext	\'95	}PNET exclusion\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}For this reboostrap, PNET OC will be purposely excluded:\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	
\f6\i\b NO
\f2\i0\b0  reset / redeploy of OIR and OIF switches / firewalls (as long as they are at 1.14.6). \
{\listtext	2.	}2.	
\f6\i\b NO
\f2\i0\b0  change in FW rules on OIR or OIF sides\
{\listtext	3.	}3.	
\f6\i\b NO
\f2\i0\b0  change in subnetting / VLANs / DHCP helpers\
{\listtext	4.	}4.	All OIC VMs will be redeployed with the same IP they had before\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs24 \cf11 {\listtext	5.	}Data collection\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	Ensure that the customer\'92s \cf12 ocinfo.common file is saved to a secure location 
\f6\i\b external to the OIR
\f2\i0\b0 \cf0  (all data will be destroyed on the OIR, for example use removable media or transcribed to paper if removable media is not an option). This is to ensure that the team bootstrapping OICv1 has a reference to all OIR subnets.\
{\listtext	2.	}2.	\cf12 Collect all OIC and OIF switch and firewall credentials, store them in a secure location 
\f6\i\b external to the OIR
\f2\i0\b0 \cf0  (all data will be destroyed on the OIR, for example use removable media or transcribed to paper if removable media is not an option)\
{\listtext	3.	}3.	\cf12 Collect and store all OIR iLO credentials 
\f6\i\b external to the OIR
\f2\i0\b0 \cf0  (all data will be destroyed on the OIR, for example on removable media or transcribed to paper if removable media is not an option), while we will be performing changes on HW configuration of BM hosts, iLO credentials are not required to change unless it covers a customer compliance task.\
{\listtext	4.	}4.	\cf12 Collaborate with the customer to collect any log (e.g. Splunk) or other data that the customer requires and save to a secure location 
\f6\i\b external to the OIR
\f2\i0\b0 \cf0  (all data will be destroyed on the OIR, for example on removable media or transcribed to paper if removable media is not an option).\
{\listtext	5.	}5.	\cf12 (Optional) Collect config.ps1 from the CONFIG1 VM and store in a secure location 
\f6\i\b external to the OIR
\f2\i0\b0 \cf0  (all data will be destroyed on the OIR, for example use removable media or transcribed to paper if removable media is not an option) to use as a reference.\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs24 \cf11 {\listtext	6.	}Procedure\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	Validate that the OIR and OIF switches and firewalls are up to date per product definition.\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	a.	}a.	\cf12 This will require an interaction with the PNET team to validate that the correct version is applied.\cf0 \
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	2.	}2.	\cf12 Start the OIR rebootstrap at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.cloud.google.com/distributed-cloud/hosted/docs/latest/gdcag/infrastructure/operations-center-setup-30/setup-bootstrap#hyper-v-setup"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 Hyper-V hosts bootstrap and setup (bare metal hosts)}} step\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0
